e got to give yourself a chance i  said all right and i went and i showed  up and i wouldn't leave i wouldn't leave  the lobby of the hotel until i met  everybody and i'd gone to that  convention for 40 consecutive years  40 consecutive years one of my buddies  who i met at the convention dick  robertson he ran warner brothers warner  brothers television distribution right  brought in a couple of billion a year so  i'm out at his beach house in malibu and  we're out on his deck and we're looking  out at the ocean drinking lemonade and  he's got a couple of labs and i'm  petting labs and he just casually says  to me yeah you know that television show  that once a week one hour tv show that  we syndicate called hbo comedy hour  where they would take comedians doing  their their specials he goes i gave that  show to a friend of ours i go why'd you  give give that show to a friend of yours  he said because that's a once a week  show that only brings in 10 million a  year and he says and i have my sales  people going out on the road to bring it  to do the first cycle of friends  and i expect them to come back like with  a billion dollars and i don't want them  he said quote  messing around with a once a week show  that only brings in 10  million a year and he was like hmm and i  and i said  wow okay  and i went home and the next day i  started my company from my dining room  table selling a once a week one-hour  show chasing a once-a-week one-hour show  that could bring in 10 million a year  that and i was like i'm gonna take  studio crumbs and i'm gonna make a  gourmet meal  how has it been with family and friends  over the years like as far as support  going from one one stage of your career  to the next you know it's so funny  johnny carson said you know what happens  is you know when you start to have  success he goes you don't change the  people around you change  and so i learned early on okay i got to  go a little i got to go the extra mile  make them comfortable 